# DeepSeek Provider Rules

Docs: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/  
Pricing: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing  
OpenAI-compat shapes: `` (local reference; do not vendor)

**Base URL (OpenAI format) default:** `https://api.deepseek.com` — see
`internal/config/urls.go`.  
(Anthropic-compat URL exists upstream; **MVP uses OpenAI chat completions only**.)

## Supported models (MVP)

| API model ID | Role |
| ---- | --- |
| `deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp` | Cheap / high-volume execution; **native vision** (https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/vision) |
| `deepseek-v4-pro` | Harder reasoning / agentic execution (text-only; images described via flash-vision-exp) |
| `deepseek-v4-flash` | Legacy id; resolves to `deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp` |

**Deprecated aliases (upstream, do not prefer in our map):** `deepseek-chat`,
`deepseek-reasoner` (historically flash non-thinking / thinking; sunset
2026-07-24 UTC per DeepSeek docs). Prefer `deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp` /
`deepseek-v4-pro`.

Images are supported **only** on `deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp` (user messages).
Other DeepSeek models return 400 "This model does not support image".

## Thinking / sampling (MVP)

| Concern | Guidance |
| ---- | --- |
| Thinking | Prefer explicit `thinking: {"type":"enabled"\|"disabled"}` (+ optional `reasoning_effort`) per DeepSeek docs — **do not** apply Moonshot K2 `thinking` or K3-only `reasoning_effort` semantics blindly |
| Tools / JSON | Supported on v4 flash & pro — still run gateway sanitizer for Cursor quirks |
| Streaming | OpenAI-compatible SSE family; separate reasoning vs content when present |
| Auth | `Authorization: Bearer {DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}` only |

Official first call: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/

## Out of MVP (document only)

- Anthropic Messages base URL (`/anthropic`) — not the Cursor OpenAI override path
- FIM / chat-prefix beta endpoints unless a later task adds them

### `DeepSeek thinking param mismatch`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| 400 / unexpected thinking on v4 | Sent Moonshot-only params or omitted DeepSeek `thinking` object | Apply **provider-aware** sanitize from model map (`deepseek` row); see `gateway.mdc` |

### `Routed to DeepSeek without API key`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| Upstream 401 after alias maps to DeepSeek | Only Moonshot key saved | Require `deepseekKeyEncrypted` when resolved provider is `deepseek` (doctor / set-key) |

### `Downgraded flash turns are nearly free via prompt cache`

In a multi-turn agent flow, the conversation context grows monotonically, so
every successive tool-result request re-sends nearly the whole prior context.
DeepSeek auto-caches this prefix, making iterated cheap turns extraordinarily
cheap.

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| `deepseek-v4-flash` tool-result turns log `est_usd ≈ 0.000` with ~99% `cache_hit_tokens` (e.g. 40,576 hit / 46 miss) while `tokens_in` climbs each turn | DeepSeek prompt caching keys on a matching prefix; because each turn appends one tool result to unchanged prior messages, the prefix (and thus the cache) is reused | Expected and desirable — do not treat near-zero flash-cost turns in a stable conversation as under-counting. It means the per-turn downgrade is already paying for itself; run medium write-turns on `pro` and small/read-only on `flash` without fear of cost blow-up |

### `DeepSeek 400 This model does not support image`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| Upstream 400 on `deepseek-v4-pro` (or OpenRouter DeepSeek flash) with screenshots in history | Only `deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp` accepts `image_url`; images only in `user` messages | Native passthrough on vision-exp (`HasNativeVision`). Pro and OR flash twins go through the describer after router/peak (`applyVision` in `proxy.go`) |

